I'll be home tomorrow.</i>

503
00:39:05.120 --> 00:39:07.120
All right. See you.

504
00:39:08.040 --> 00:39:09.640
Bye. love.

505
00:39:15.520 --> 00:39:18.120
Is my investigation being set up to fail?

506
00:39:20.760 --> 00:39:21.760
Why?

507
00:39:26.840 --> 00:39:28.440
If someone's pressuring you...

508
00:39:39.320 --> 00:39:41.000
They aren't pressuring me.

509
00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:43.800
They're threatening me.

510
00:39:48.600 --> 00:39:50.056
Rhys.

511
00:39:50.080 --> 00:39:53.016
if you want to carry on being a
policeman when this is all over.

512
00:39:53.040 --> 00:39:55.776
find a reason to excuse
yourself from the case

513
00:39:55.800 --> 00:39:59.120
that doesn't point suspicion
my way. then step away.

514
00:39:59.680 --> 00:40:03.216
I cannot guarantee that
whoever is in charge of this case

515
00:40:03.240 --> 00:40:04.960
will come out of it in one piece.

516
00:40:05.640 --> 00:40:07.280
Especially someone like you.

517
00:40:11.280 --> 00:40:12.560
Someone like me?

518
00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:17.720
A man with debts.

519
00:40:21.400 --> 00:40:23.280
Is this why I was picked for this?

520
00:40:24.320 --> 00:40:25.576
To be the fall guy?

521
00:40:25.600 --> 00:40:26.800
Don't be so bloody paranoid.

522
00:40:29.280 --> 00:40:30.280
But your...

523
00:40:31.960 --> 00:40:32.960
Problem...

524
00:40:33.880 --> 00:40:35.360
Will come out in the wash.

525
00:40:39.200 --> 00:40:40.320
Resign the case.

526
00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:45.120
It's the only way you're
going to survive this.

527
00:41:16.040 --> 00:41:17.480
Going somewhere?

528
00:41:19.240 --> 00:41:22.096
Jesus. you scared the shit out
of me. I thought you were at work.

529
00:41:22.120 --> 00:41:24.920
Yeah. and I thought you
were coming round tomorrow.

530
00:41:27.800 --> 00:41:29.440
It's not up there any more.

531
00:41:36.080 --> 00:41:37.600
I'm not stupid. Zara.

532
00:41:38.520 --> 00:41:39.600
Fuck's sake.

533
00:41:40.440 --> 00:41:44.176
I haven't seen you in months.
and then you turn up out of the blue

534
00:41:44.200 --> 00:41:46.616
the day after your
company's been robbed?

535
00:41:46.640 --> 00:41:49.976
It's funny to think there's
been four billion quid

536
00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:53.040
stashed under my floorboards.
and I didn't have a clue.

537
00:41:54.200 --> 00:41:55.496
It's not four billion.

538
00:41:55.520 --> 00:41:58.080
Well. I looked up what a cold wallet is.

539
00:41:58.920 --> 00:42:01.000
Spent all afternoon researching it.

540
00:42:01.960 --> 00:42:03.160
So how much is on it?

541
00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:07.416
Well. if you read up.
then you would know

542
00:42:07.440 --> 00:42:09.656
that you can't get into it
without my passwords.

543
00:42:09.680 --> 00:42:11.496
It's worthless without
my passwords. actually.

544
00:42:11.520 --> 00:42:16.400
Right. And your passwords are
worthless without the cold wallet.

545
00:42:17.040 --> 00:42:19.320
So. here we are.

546
00:42:21.960 --> 00:42:22.960
Okay.

547
00:42:31.680 --> 00:42:32.680
What do you want?

548
00:42:36.240 --> 00:42:37.320
What do you think I want?

549
00:42:39.240 --> 00:42:41.640
Storage fees.

550
00:42:46.480 --> 00:42:51.176
The people that I am dealing with.
I think... I think they want me dead.

551
00:42:51.200 --> 00:42:54.416
- I don't know. they were chasing me and...
- you brought them here?

552
00:42:54.440 --> 00:42:55.936
- Well. I was trying...
- Nice.

553
00:42:55.960 --> 00:42:57.256
To do a deal with them.

554
00:42:57.280 --> 00:43:01.160
Mum. please. please. I
need the cold wallet so I...

555
00:43:02.480 --> 00:43:04.096
Get out of the country.

556
00:43:04.120 --> 00:43:07.816
I can't do it without the money.
so I need it. So please give it to me.

557
00:43:07.840 --> 00:43:08.840
And then...

558
00:43:09.840 --> 00:43:13.080
And then when it's all calmed
down. yes. I will sort you out.

559
00:43:13.760 --> 00:43:14.760
Wow.

560
00:43:15.400 --> 00:43:18.360
You've really bitten off more
than you can chew. haven't you?

561
00:43:20.120 --> 00:43:21.680
Look.

562
00:43:22.320 --> 00:43:24.680
love. I give you that cold wallet.

563
00:43:25.440 --> 00:43:27.520
you're off to Brazil and
I never see you again.

564
00:43:37.040 --> 00:43:38.920
I don't fucking believe you.

565
00:43:43.320 --> 00:43:45.296
Come on. How much is
on it? You can at least...

566
00:43:45.320 --> 00:43:47.440
You can at least tell me that much.

567
00:43:48.920 --> 00:43:51.480
A million. Depending
on the exchange rate.

568
00:43:52.080 --> 00:43:54.616
What. they steal. you know. four billion.

569
00:43:54.640 --> 00:43:56.936
and they give you what.
one million? I don't think so.

570
00:43:56.960 --> 00:43:59.576
- Come on. How much?
- Five. Five million.

571
00:43:59.600 --> 00:44:02.120
Five? Wow!

572
00:44:03.200 --> 00:44:06.136
My maths was never my strong point.

573
00:44:06.160 --> 00:44:11.256
but I would say for a very
reasonable 20% storage fees...

574
00:44:11.280 --> 00:44:14.096
- i...
- come on. you give me one million.

575
00:44:14.120 --> 00:44:16.896
You get to keep the other four million.

576
00:44:16.920 --> 00:44:19.736
- Everybody's happy.
- Mum. you are not getting a million quid.

577
00:44:19.760 --> 00:44:22.256
You're gonna end up blowing through
it. and we'll both end up arrested.

578
00:44:22.280 --> 00:44:26.296
Come on. darling. Look. you've
got to learn to trust me more.

579
00:44:26.320 --> 00:44:29.696
What. because you have
done so much to earn my trust!

580
00:44:29.720 --> 00:44:34.136
Don't fucking get all high
and mighty with me. Zara!

581
00:44:34.160 --> 00:44:38.456
Just take a guess who the
hospital has all its pensions with.

582
00:44:38.480 --> 00:44:41.536
You have stolen your own
fucking mother's pension!

583
00:44:41.560 --> 00:44:44.016
So don't turn your
fucking nose up at me.

584
00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:46.840
You've been doing it since you
were a kid. and I'm fucking sick of it.

585
00:44:48.520 --> 00:44:50.816
Yeah. you just... just go home.

586
00:44:50.840 --> 00:44:53.696
calm down and then. you know.

587
00:44:53.720 --> 00:44:57.376
give me a call in a few days and
we'll work something out. okay?

588
00:44:57.400 --> 00:44:58.520
You don't get it. mum.

589
00:44:59.280 --> 00:45:01.920
After tonight. I won't
be alive in a few days.

590
00:45:44.760 --> 00:45:45.760
Get in!

591
00:45:52.920 --> 00:45:54.120
Are you okay?

592
00:45:55.440 --> 00:45:56.440
Thank you.

593
00:45:58.280 --> 00:46:00.016
I feel like such a fucking idiot.

594
00:46:00.040 --> 00:46:02.896
I was trying to reason with
them. Give them a peace offering.

595
00:46:02.920 --> 00:46:04.520
- Fuck!
- Who's "them"?

596
00:46:07.280 --> 00:46:08.280
The thieves.

597
00:46:11.640 --> 00:46:14.000
Zara. that wasn't a thief
trying to pick you up back there.

598
00:46:14.840 --> 00:46:16.240
Who else would it be?

599
00:46:17.360 --> 00:46:18.560
It was MI5.

599
00:46:19.305 --> 00:47:19.712
